# /sdd-trace

Purpose:
  Bidirectional traceability from requirement to proof and back.

Owns: commands/sdd-trace.sdd

Description:
  Traces forward (requirement → decision → task → code → test → proof)
  and reverse (code → task → decision → requirement). Uses compact IDs
  (R, D, T, C, X, P prefixes) for human-readable trace chains.

Usage:
  /sdd-trace --forward <R<id>|D<id>|T<id>|C<id>|X<id>|P<id>>
  /sdd-trace --reverse <file-path>
  /sdd-trace --coverage

Options:
  --forward  Trace forward from entity ID
  --reverse  Trace reverse from code file path
  --coverage Show requirement/test/proof coverage ratios

Mode: READ_ONLY

Output:
  TRACE CHAIN

    Direction: <forward | reverse>
    Start:     <R101 | /src/payment/service.ts>
    Chain:
      [R101] requirement: payment-refund-idempotency
        → [D202] decision: use idempotency key
          → [T303] task: implement refund idempotency
            → [C404] code: internal/payment/service.go
              → [X505] test: TestRefundIdempotency
                → [P606] proof: PASS (test suite)

    Coverage:
      Requirements: 100
      Implemented:  96
      Tested:       91
      Verified:     87
      Coverage:     87%

Rules:
  [TRC-01] /sdd-trace MUST show full chain or report BREAK.
  [TRC-02] /sdd-trace MUST include confidence for inferred links.
  [TRC-03] /sdd-trace coverage MUST count verified items only.

Navigation:
  INDEX: @INDEX.sdd
  Queries: @../queries/traceability.sdd
  EpistemicEntities: @../concepts/epistemic-entities.sdd
  Decisions: @../decisions/INDEX.sdd

State: +
